<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Bouygues started outperform.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Bouygues started outperform.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lehman Brothers said analyst Paul Chambers started coverage of offshore construction company Bouygues Offshore SA with an outperform rating.</p>
<p>-- Lehman was the lead underwriter of the French company's November IPO. It went public at 12-3/8.</p>
<p>-- Shares rose 1/8 to 12-1/2.</p>
<p>-- Lehman said Bouygues could trade at 13.5 times Lehman's 1998 estimate of $1.18 a share over the next 15 months, or $16 a share.</p>
<p>-- Chambers expects the company to earn $1.02 in 1997.</p>
</text>
